1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,616
Our project studies few-shot industrial anomaly
detection. In manufacturing, normal product
images are easier to

2
00:00:06,696 --> 00:00:13,313
collect than examples of every possible defect.
We use the VisA dataset to ask whether

3
00:00:13,393 --> 00:00:20,009
a few normal reference images can help detect and
locate an anomaly in a new

4
00:00:20,089 --> 00:00:24,920
product image. The outlines on the right show the
annotated defects.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,442
We have implemented two approaches. Part One is a
template-difference baseline. It selects the
nearest

6
00:00:31,522 --> 00:00:37,963
normal template and computes an RGB difference
map. Part Two uses frozen DINOv2 features and

7
00:00:38,043 --> 00:00:44,485
a memory bank of normal image patches. A test
patch is scored by its distance

8
00:00:44,565 --> 00:00:51,007
from the nearest normal feature. Both methods use
the same reference and test manifest. We

9
00:00:51,087 --> 00:00:57,529
reserve twenty additional normal training images
per category for threshold calibration only.
These images are

10
00:00:57,609 --> 00:01:04,050
excluded from the reference bank and test set. We
do not train the methods using

11
00:01:04,130 --> 00:01:04,920
defect labels.

12
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:12,630
Part One is implemented and has completed all one
hundred and fifty test images in

13
00:01:12,710 --> 00:01:20,341
our first cashew configuration, using one
reference image and seed zero. It outputs the
selected

14
00:01:20,421 --> 00:01:28,051
template, an anomaly map, a continuous score, and
an OK or NG decision. Here is

15
00:01:28,131 --> 00:01:35,761
a genuine failure. This defective image receives
a score of about zero point four nine

16
00:01:35,841 --> 00:01:43,471
eight, below its calibrated threshold of about
zero point six one. It is therefore classified

17
00:01:43,551 --> 00:01:51,182
as OK. Strong responses appear around the product
outline, rather than only at the annotated

18
00:01:51,262 --> 00:01:58,892
defects. This suggests sensitivity to normal
appearance or position changes, although
confirming the cause requires

19
00:01:58,972 --> 00:01:59,920
